## Soundness posture (see soundness.md)

C3C is NOT a sound vehicle - it only isolates the per-limb slice. A per-limb aggregate
bound redesign (Spec A) is binding-invariant: the 12 per-limb range calls it replaces
are NOT part of the I15 witness shape (CT0 relation relies on |e0| < q_l, which is in
the flat e0 polynomial, not the per-limb pk/r1/r2/p1/p2). Spec B (also aggregate r1/r2)
is NOT recommended - it re-opens I15 adjudication.

## Verdict

Per-limb slice of C3's range family RAN = 966,604 g = 32.59% of C3 leaf = 8.37% of the
DKG base (byte-twin with r146 for the family ceiling). The aggregate-bound lever's
maximum attainable is this 8.37%; after an in-tree Spec-A proto + e2e it should land
≈ 6-7% DKG base (the per-limb wire overhead that survives after aggregation is not
zero). In-tree delivery is owner-gated per the 2026-09-12 C6-class sign-off.

